BT /F1 9.0 Tf 45 528.0 Td (#### Q1: Why did you choose FastAPI over Django or Flask for the backend?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 45 516.0 Td (**Answer**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 45 504.0 Td (1. **Asynchronous Execution \(`async`/`await`\)**: LectureLens performs high-concurrency I/O) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 45 492.0 Td (\(database queries, video streaming, external API calls\) alongside heavy background task) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 45 480.0 Td (scheduling. FastAPI natively handles asynchronous concurrency without blocking worker threads.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 45 468.0 Td (2. **In-Process Python AI Ecosystem**: In-process execution of Faster-Whisper, PyTorch, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 45 456.0 Td (Sentence-Transformers requires a Python environment. Frameworks in other languages \(Node.js,) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 45 444.0 Td (Go\) would require complex IPC or microservice wrappers.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 45 432.0 Td (3. **Pydantic Validation & Auto-Documentation**: Pydantic v2 enforces strict runtime data) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 45 420.0 Td (validation and automatically generates interactive OpenAPI/Swagger documentation at `/docs`.) Tj ET
0.8 w 0.8 0.8 0.8 RG 45 402.0 m 567 402.0 l S
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 45 386.0 Td (#### Q2: Why use MongoDB Atlas instead of a traditional relational database \(PostgreSQL\) or a) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 45 374.0 Td (dedicated vector database \(Pinecone\)?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 45 362.0 Td (**Answer**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 45 350.0 Td (1. **Unified Storage Tier**: MongoDB Atlas provides both flexible document storage \(courses,) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 45 338.0 Td (nested transcript segments, audit logs\) and dense vector search \(`vectorSearch`\) in a single) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 45 326.0 Td (managed cluster. This eliminates the operational overhead, data synchronization lag, and extra) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 45 314.0 Td (cost of running two separate databases.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 45 302.0 Td (2. **Natural Document Hierarchy**: Spoken lectures naturally form hierarchical structures) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 45 290.0 Td (\(lectures contain segments; segments group into topics; topics have summaries and quizzes\). In) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 45 278.0 Td (MongoDB, these map naturally to nested BSON documents without complex multi-table SQL joins.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 45 266.0 Td (3. **Course-Filtered Vector Search**: Atlas Search supports pre-filtering vectors on metadata) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 45 254.0 Td (fields \(`course_id`, `is_published`\) during the nearest-neighbor search, ensuring students only) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 45 242.0 Td (retrieve content from courses they are enrolled in.) Tj ET
0.8 w 0.8 0.8 0.8 RG 45 224.0 m 567 224.0 l S
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 45 208.0 Td (#### Q3: How does the video player synchronize with the transcript bidirectionally?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 45 196.0 Td (**Answer**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 45 184.0 Td (1. **Video to Transcript**: The video player emits high-frequency time update events) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 45 172.0 Td (\(`timeupdate` on HTML5 `<video>`, or a 250ms polling loop on the YouTube IFrame API\). The) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 45 160.0 Td (component finds the segment where \\start \\le t_{\\current < \\end, marks it as active, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 45 148.0 Td (invokes `scrollIntoView\({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'nearest' \)`.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 45 136.0 Td (2. **Transcript to Video**: Each paragraph and segment displays its timestamp. Clicking a) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 45 124.0 Td (segment triggers an imperative call to the player ref: `videoRef.current.currentTime =) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 45 112.0 Td (targetTime` \(or `player.seekTo\(targetTime\)` for YouTube\).) Tj ET
