BT /F1 9.0 Tf 45 730.0 Td (#### Q4: How does your Topic Segmentation algorithm work, and why is it superior to fixed-time) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 45 718.0 Td (windows?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 45 706.0 Td (**Answer**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 45 694.0 Td (Fixed-time windows \(e.g., slicing every 5 minutes\) cut arbitrarily across mid-sentence) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 45 682.0 Td (explanations. LectureLens implements **semantic boundary clustering**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 45 670.0 Td (1. Each segment text is embedded into a 384-dimensional vector using `paraphrase-multilingual-) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 45 658.0 Td (MiniLM-L12-v2`.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 45 646.0 Td (2. We compute cosine similarity between adjacent segment vectors:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 45 634.0 Td (   \\sim\(\\e_{i-1, \\e_i\) = \\\\e_{i-1 \\cdot \\e_i{\\|\\e_{i-1\\| \\|\\e_i\\|) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 45 622.0 Td (3. When similarity drops below \\theta = 0.45 after a minimum cluster size of 3 segments, a) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 45 610.0 Td (topic boundary is placed.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 45 598.0 Td (4. In academic benchmarks against human-annotated ground truth, semantic segmentation achieved) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 45 586.0 Td (an **F1-score of 100.0%** \(within \\pm 45s tolerance\), whereas a fixed-window baseline scored) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 45 574.0 Td (**0.0%**.) Tj ET
0.8 w 0.8 0.8 0.8 RG 45 556.0 m 567 556.0 l S
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 45 540.0 Td (#### Q5: What is Retrieval-Augmented Generation \(RAG\), and how does LectureLens prevent) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 45 528.0 Td (hallucinations?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 45 516.0 Td (**Answer**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 45 504.0 Td (RAG is an AI pattern where an information retrieval system searches an authoritative corpus for) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 45 492.0 Td (relevant facts and provides them as context to a language model to synthesize an answer.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 45 480.0 Td (LectureLens prevents hallucinations through three mechanisms:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 45 468.0 Td (1. **Deterministic Context**: The answer is synthesized strictly from retrieved lecture chunks,) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 45 456.0 Td (not from unconstrained model memory.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 45 444.0 Td (2. **Abstention Cutoff Gate**: If the top cosine similarity score is below **0.30**, the system) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 45 432.0 Td (abstains honestly rather than guessing: *"The available lecture materials do not contain) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 45 420.0 Td (sufficient evidence to answer this question reliably."*) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 45 408.0 Td (3. **Verifiable Citations**: Every answer provides clickable timestamps linking directly to the) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 45 396.0 Td (spoken proof in the video recording.) Tj ET
0.8 w 0.8 0.8 0.8 RG 45 378.0 m 567 378.0 l S
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 45 362.0 Td (#### Q6: Why did you select `paraphrase-multilingual-MiniLM-L12-v2` for embeddings?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 45 350.0 Td (**Answer**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 45 338.0 Td (1. **Bilingual Competence**: It is trained on parallel sentence corpora across 50+ languages,) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 45 326.0 Td (including English and Hindi, allowing it to align conceptual meanings in bilingual and Hinglish) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 45 314.0 Td (lectures.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 45 302.0 Td (2. **Compact Dimensionality**: At 384 dimensions, vector embeddings consume minimal memory and) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 45 290.0 Td (compute during cosine nearest-neighbor search compared to 1536-dimensional models \(like OpenAI) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 45 278.0 Td (`text-embedding-3-small`\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 45 266.0 Td (3. **Fast CPU Inference**: The model runs efficiently on standard CPU hardware without) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 45 254.0 Td (requiring dedicated GPU infrastructure.) Tj ET
0.8 w 0.8 0.8 0.8 RG 45 236.0 m 567 236.0 l S
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 45 220.0 Td (#### Q7: What is Reciprocal Rank Fusion \(RRF\), and why is it used in Hybrid Search?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 45 208.0 Td (**Answer**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 45 196.0 Td (Different search strategies excel at different query types:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 45 184.0 Td (- **Vector Search** excels at conceptual queries \(*"how do models learn from errors?"*) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 45 172.0 Td (\\rightarrow matches *backpropagation*\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 45 160.0 Td (- **BM25 Lexical Search** excels at exact acronyms and identifier names \(*"DDL"*, *"CS401"*\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 45 142.0 Td (Hybrid Search combines both rankings using **Reciprocal Rank Fusion \(RRF\)**:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 45 124.0 Td (\\RRF\\_Score\(d\) = \\sum_{m \\in \\{\\vector, \\keyword\\ \\1{k + \\rank_m\(d\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 45 106.0 Td (Where k = 60 is a smoothing constant. This ensures documents appearing near the top of either) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.0 Tf 45 94.0 Td (or both search modalities receive balanced, robust rankings.) Tj ET
0.8 w 0.8 0.8 0.8 RG 45 76.0 m 567 76.0 l S
